{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":"2026-10-23T04:00:35.135Z","tool_name":"run_shell_command","tool_id":"run_shell_command__call_283367","parameters":{"command":"echo \"- $(date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ) [argon] starting: running fast backtracking / SAT solver for small K and analyzing structural properties of internal/external stability.\" >> /work/board.md\npython3 -c '\ndef dominates(x, y):\n    return (x[0] > y[0] and x[1] > y[1]) or (x[0] > y[0] and x[2] > y[2]) or (x[1] > y[1] and x[2] > y[2])\n\ndef solve(K):\n    pts = [(a, b, K - a - b) for a in range(K + 1) for b in range(K + 1 - a)]\n    n = len(pts)\n    dom_by = [set() for _ in range(n)]\n    doms = [set() for _ in range(n)]\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(n):\n            if dominates(pts[i], pts[j]):\n                doms[i].add(j)\n                dom_by[j].add(i)\n    \n    # Note: domination is symmetric? Wait: x dominates y iff 2 coords of x > y.\n    # Since sum(x) = sum(y) = K, if x has 2 coords > y, then the 3rd coord of x must be < y!\n    # So x cannot be dominated by y at the same time? Wait: can x dominate y AND y dominate x?\n    # No, because x has 2 coords > y and 1 coord < y, so y has only 1 coord > x.\n    # Thus domination is an oriented graph (in fact, a tournament-like graph, except when coords are equal!).\n    # Wait: what if x and y share a coordinate? If x_0 = y_0, then since sum = K, one of {1,2} has x > y and one has x < y.\n    # So two points have NO domination between them iff they share at least one coordinate!\n    \n    # Wait! Let us check that!\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i+1, n):\n            same_coord = (pts[i][0] == pts[j][0]) or (pts[i][1] == pts[j][1]) or (pts[i][2] == pts[j][2])\n            neither = (j not in doms[i]) and (i not in doms[j])\n            assert same_coord == neither\n    print(f\"K={K}: verified that x, y are incomparable iff they share a coordinate!\")\nsolve(5)\n'","description":"Append status to board.md and verify the characterization of incomparability under domination."}}
